  "result": "`python3 -m shop quote a:12.5:2` should now print 27.06, and the test suite passes.\n\n**Root cause:** `to_cents` in `shop/money.py` padded the fractional part on the wrong side. It used `frac.rjust(2, \"0\")`, so `\"5\"` became `\"05\"` and `12.5` was read as 12.05 (1205 cents) instead of 12.50 (1250 cents). The quote then came out as 26.09 instead of 27.06.\n\n**Fix:** Changed `rjust` to `ljust` on that line, so `\"5\"` becomes `\"50\"`. Nothing else changed.\n\n**Checks:**\n- `python3 -c \"from shop.cli import main; main(['quote','a:12.5:2'])\"` prints `27.06`.\n- `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -t .` ran 6 tests, all OK.\n\nThe `python3 -m shop` form was not tried, since the repo has no `__main__.py`, as you said. The existing tests don't cover a single-digit fraction like `12.5`, so a regression test for that case would be a sensible addition. I did not add one.",
